      ],
      "quality": "unverified",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "evidence_id": "ev-simon-sinek-start-with-why-c002",
          "source_id": "src-simon-sinek-start-with-why",
          "source_version": "98ca065cced77c6372fbf4f23256f0759c017fd1abc5f5e111894c8d5c640288",
          "locator": {
            "kind": "page",
            "value": "p. 17"
          },
          "kind": "concept",
          "mark": "paraphrase",
          "original_speaker": null,
          "excerpt": null,
          "paraphrase": "Most organizations cannot say why their customers choose them or why their employees stay. They know what they do, and sometimes how they do it, but the cause underneath is unstated, so decisions default to features and price.",
          "claim_ids": [],
          "seat_id": "simon-sinek"
        },
        {
          "evidence_id": "ev-simon-sinek-start-with-why-c003",
          "source_id": "src-simon-sinek-start-with-why",
          "source_version": "98ca065cced77c6372fbf4f23256f0759c017fd1abc5f5e111894c8d5c640288",
          "locator": {
            "kind": "page",
            "value": "p. 42"
          },
          "kind": "concept",
          "mark": "paraphrase",
          "original_speaker": null,
          "excerpt": null,
          "paraphrase": "The root problem is direction of communication: people and companies speak from the outside in, leading with products and features, and fall back on manipulations such as price cuts, promotions, fear, and novelty because they do not understand how decisions form around belief and feeling.",
          "claim_ids": [],
          "seat_id": "simon-sinek"
        },
        {
          "evidence_id": "ev-simon-sinek-start-with-why-c004",
          "source_id": "src-simon-sinek-start-with-why",
          "source_version": "98ca065cced77c6372fbf4f23256f0759c017fd1abc5f5e111894c8d5c640288",
          "locator": {
            "kind": "page",
            "value": "p. 41"
          },
          "kind": "concept",
          "mark": "paraphrase",
          "original_speaker": null,
          "excerpt": null,
          "paraphrase": "The Golden Circle is a three-level model: WHY, the purpose, cause, or belief; HOW, the actions and principles that realize it; WHAT, the products and results. Clarity of WHY comes first, and very few organizations can articulate theirs.",
          "claim_ids": [],
          "seat_id": "simon-sinek"
        },
        {
          "evidence_id": "ev-simon-sinek-start-with-why-c005",
          "source_id": "src-simon-sinek-start-with-why",
          "source_version": "98ca065cced77c6372fbf4f23256f0759c017fd1abc5f5e111894c8d5c640288",
          "locator": {
            "kind": "page",
            "value": "p. 18"
          },
          "kind": "concept",
          "mark": "paraphrase",
          "original_speaker": null,
          "excerpt": null,
          "paraphrase": "The foundational principle: people respond to why something exists, its purpose and cause, before they respond to what it is. Trust and loyalty follow a belief made visible in action, not a longer feature list.",
          "claim_ids": [],
          "seat_id": "simon-sinek"
        },
        {
          "evidence_id": "ev-simon-sinek-start-with-why-c006",
          "source_id": "src-simon-sinek-start-with-why",
          "source_version": "98ca065cced77c6372fbf4f23256f0759c017fd1abc5f5e111894c8d5c640288",
          "locator": {
            "kind": "page",
            "value": "p. 18"
          },
          "kind": "concept",
          "mark": "paraphrase",
          "original_speaker": null,
          "excerpt": null,
          "paraphrase": "The transformation the book describes runs from manipulation-driven transactions, bought with price, promotions, fear, peer pressure, or novelty, toward inspiration-driven loyalty, where customers and employees stay because they believe what the organization believes.",
          "claim_ids": [],
          "seat_id": "simon-sinek"
        },
        {
          "evidence_id": "ev-simon-sinek-start-with-why-c007",
          "source_id": "src-simon-sinek-start-with-why",
          "source_version": "98ca065cced77c6372fbf4f23256f0759c017fd1abc5f5e111894c8d5c640288",
          "locator": {
            "kind": "page",
            "value": "p. 41"
          },
          "kind": "concept",
          "mark": "paraphrase",
          "original_speaker": null,
          "excerpt": null,
          "paraphrase": "The book works through pointed questions that force a leader to state a cause: why the work exists, why anyone should care, and why customers and employees chose this organization over another.",
          "claim_ids": [],
          "seat_id": "simon-sinek"
        },
        {
          "evidence_id": "ev-simon-sinek-start-with-why-c008",
          "source_id": "src-simon-sinek-start-with-why",
          "source_version": "98ca065cced77c6372fbf4f23256f0759c017fd1abc5f5e111894c8d5c640288",
          "locator": {
            "kind": "page",
            "value": "p. 42"
          },
          "kind": "concept",
          "mark": "paraphrase",
          "original_speaker": null,
          "excerpt": null,
          "paraphrase": "The Golden Circle diagram, three concentric levels with WHY at the center, is the working tool: a map for testing messages, offers, hires, and decisions against the stated purpose before anything ships.",
          "claim_ids": [],
          "seat_id": "simon-sinek"
        },
        {
          "evidence_id": "ev-simon-sinek-start-with-why-c009",
          "source_id": "src-simon-sinek-start-with-why",
          "source_version": "98ca065cced77c6372fbf4f23256f0759c017fd1abc5f5e111894c8d5c640288",
          "locator": {
            "kind": "page",
            "value": "p. 52"
          },
          "kind": "concept",
          "mark": "paraphrase",
          "original_speaker": null,
          "excerpt": null,
          "paraphrase": "Objections based on product quality are answered by separating levels: quality is a WHAT. Good products matter, but a good product alone does not explain why customers stay loyal when a competitor matches it.",
          "claim_ids": [],
          "seat_id": "simon-sinek"
        },
        {
          "evidence_id": "ev-simon-sinek-start-with-why-c010",
          "source_id": "src-simon-sinek-start-with-why",
          "source_version": "98ca065cced77c6372fbf4f23256f0759c017fd1abc5f5e111894c8d5c640288",
          "locator": {
            "kind": "page",
            "value": "p. 82"
          },
          "kind": "concept",
          "mark": "paraphrase",
          "original_speaker": null,
          "excerpt": null,
          "paraphrase": "The teaching voice uses short declarative claims, deliberate repetition of the central principle, and named contrasts, leaders versus those who lead, manipulation versus inspiration, so the idea stays portable and testable.",
          "claim_ids": [],
          "seat_id": "simon-sinek"
        },
        {
          "evidence_id": "ev-simon-sinek-start-with-why-c012",
          "source_id": "src-simon-sinek-start-with-why",
          "source_version": "98ca065cced77c6372fbf4f23256f0759c017fd1abc5f5e111894c8d5c640288",
          "locator": {
            "kind": "page",
            "value": "p. 15"
          },
          "kind": "concept",
          "mark": "paraphrase",
          "original_speaker": null,
          "excerpt": null,
          "paraphrase": "The repeatable application system runs in order: find clarity of WHY, align the HOW actions and the WHAT proof behind it, then use the circle as a filter for every instruction, course of action, and desired result.",
          "claim_ids": [],
          "seat_id": "simon-sinek"
        },
        {
          "evidence_id": "ev-simon-sinek-start-with-why-c013",
          "source_id": "src-simon-sinek-start-with-why",
          "source_version": "98ca065cced77c6372fbf4f23256f0759c017fd1abc5f5e111894c8d5c640288",
          "locator": {
            "kind": "page",
            "value": "p. 30"
          },
          "kind": "concept",
          "mark": "paraphrase",
          "original_speaker": null,
          "excerpt": null,
          "paraphrase": "The quality bar is loyalty, not repeat transactions: people willing to turn down a better product or a better price to keep doing business with you. Repeat business bought by discounts does not meet the bar.",
          "claim_ids": [],
          "seat_id": "simon-sinek"
        },
        {
          "evidence_id": "ev-simon-sinek-start-with-why-c014",
          "source_id": "src-simon-sinek-start-with-why",
          "source_version": "98ca065cced77c6372fbf4f23256f0759c017fd1abc5f5e111894c8d5c640288",
          "locator": {
            "kind": "page",
            "value": "p. 54"
          },
          "kind": "concept",
          "mark": "paraphrase",
          "original_speaker": null,
          "excerpt": null,
          "paraphrase": "Execution rules include never violating the WHY: when a WHY goes fuzzy, the growth, loyalty, and inspiration that produced the original success become much harder to maintain.",
          "claim_ids": [],
          "seat_id": "simon-sinek"
        },
        {
          "evidence_id": "ev-simon-sinek-start-with-why-c015",
          "source_id": "src-simon-sinek-start-with-why",
          "source_version": "98ca065cced77c6372fbf4f23256f0759c017fd1abc5f5e111894c8d5c640288",
          "locator": {
            "kind": "page",
            "value": "p. 195"
          },
          "kind": "concept",
          "mark": "paraphrase",
          "original_speaker": null,
          "excerpt": null,
          "paraphrase": "The Split is the central failure pattern: as a company grows, attention shifts from the founding WHY to measurable WHATs, purpose goes fuzzy, and the organization splits into what it does and why it stopped saying why.",
          "claim_ids": [],
          "seat_id": "simon-sinek"
        },
        {
          "evidence_id": "ev-simon-sinek-start-with-why-c016",
          "source_id": "src-simon-sinek-start-with-why",
          "source_version": "98ca065cced77c6372fbf4f23256f0759c017fd1abc5f5e111894c8d5c640288",
          "locator": {
            "kind": "page",
            "value": "p. 85"
          },
          "kind": "concept",
          "mark": "paraphrase",
          "original_speaker": null,
          "excerpt": null,
          "paraphrase": "Decision logic is the Golden Circle Filter: when the WHY is known, a decision can be tested against it directly, which gives a confidence check stronger than opinion or rank.",
          "claim_ids": [],
          "seat_id": "simon-sinek"
        },
        {
          "evidence_id": "ev-simon-sinek-start-with-why-c017",
          "source_id": "src-simon-sinek-start-with-why",
          "source_version": "98ca065cced77c6372fbf4f23256f0759c017fd1abc5f5e111894c8d5c640288",
          "locator": {
            "kind": "page",
            "value": "p. 81"
          },
          "kind": "concept",
          "mark": "paraphrase",
          "original_speaker": null,
          "excerpt": null,
          "paraphrase": "The self-review is the balance verification: authenticity means the three levels are in balance, WHY clarity, HOW discipline, and WHAT proof consistent with one another and with observed behavior.",
          "claim_ids": [],
          "seat_id": "simon-sinek"
        },
        {
          "evidence_id": "ev-simon-sinek-start-with-why-c018",
          "source_id": "src-simon-sinek-start-with-why",
          "source_version": "98ca065cced77c6372fbf4f23256f0759c017fd1abc5f5e111894c8d5c640288",
          "locator": {
            "kind": "page",
            "value": "p. 71"
          },
          "kind": "concept",
          "mark": "paraphrase",
          "original_speaker": null,
          "excerpt": null,
          "paraphrase": "Work on purpose is done when the WHY is known and stated clearly enough for others to act on it. If the organization cannot say why it does what it does, no customer or employee can say it either.",
          "claim_ids": [],
          "seat_id": "simon-sinek"
        },
        {
          "evidence_id": "ev-simon-sinek-start-with-why-c019",
          "source_id": "src-simon-sinek-start-with-why",
          "source_version": "98ca065cced77c6372fbf4f23256f0759c017fd1abc5f5e111894c8d5c640288",
          "locator": {
            "kind": "page",
            "value": "p. 41-42"
          },
          "kind": "concept",
          "mark": "paraphrase",
          "original_speaker": null,
          "excerpt": null,
          "paraphrase": "The amateur-to-expert gap is focus: amateurs fixate on WHAT, products, features, and services, while experts start from WHY, purpose, cause, and belief, and let the WHATs follow.",
          "claim_ids": [],
          "seat_id": "simon-sinek"
        },
        {
          "evidence_id": "ev-simon-sinek-start-with-why-c020",
          "source_id": "src-simon-sinek-start-with-why",
          "source_version": "98ca065cced77c6372fbf4f23256f0759c017fd1abc5f5e111894c8d5c640288",
          "locator": {
            "kind": "page",
            "value": "p. 93"
          },
          "kind": "concept",
          "mark": "paraphrase",
          "original_speaker": null,
          "excerpt": null,
          "paraphrase": "Applied professionally, the methodology starts with leadership: leading means inspiring people toward a cause, which is different from holding the highest rank. The seat uses this to test whether a decision would still make sense described as a cause people can join.",
          "claim_ids": [],
          "seat_id": "simon-sinek"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
