      ],
      "quality": "unverified",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "evidence_id": "ev-simon-sinek-find-your-why-c002",
          "source_id": "src-simon-sinek-find-your-why",
          "source_version": "858619f10c91dcd805d57e021c40d538a7507472bfbee7b6f97c8f0a4a2f8887",
          "locator": {
            "kind": "section",
            "value": "item 2: The Central Problem"
          },
          "kind": "concept",
          "mark": "paraphrase",
          "original_speaker": null,
          "excerpt": null,
          "paraphrase": "This book exists because the earlier one made the case for WHY without giving steps to find it. Its central problem is practical: how a person or team actually discovers a WHY instead of inventing a slogan.",
          "claim_ids": [],
          "seat_id": "simon-sinek"
        },
        {
          "evidence_id": "ev-simon-sinek-find-your-why-c003",
          "source_id": "src-simon-sinek-find-your-why",
          "source_version": "858619f10c91dcd805d57e021c40d538a7507472bfbee7b6f97c8f0a4a2f8887",
          "locator": {
            "kind": "section",
            "value": "item 3: The Root Cause of Human Struggle"
          },
          "kind": "concept",
          "mark": "paraphrase",
          "original_speaker": null,
          "excerpt": null,
          "paraphrase": "The root difficulty is communicative and biological: the part of the brain that handles language deals in WHAT-level facts, while feelings and gut decisions sit elsewhere, so purpose is felt before it can be said and must be drawn out through stories.",
          "claim_ids": [],
          "seat_id": "simon-sinek"
        },
        {
          "evidence_id": "ev-simon-sinek-find-your-why-c004",
          "source_id": "src-simon-sinek-find-your-why",
          "source_version": "858619f10c91dcd805d57e021c40d538a7507472bfbee7b6f97c8f0a4a2f8887",
          "locator": {
            "kind": "section",
            "value": "item 4: The Complete Methodology - Every Step"
          },
          "kind": "concept",
          "mark": "paraphrase",
          "original_speaker": null,
          "excerpt": null,
          "paraphrase": "The discovery method is a partner process: gather specific stories from your life or the organization's history, tell them to an objective partner, let the partner mine them for recurring themes, and draft a WHY statement from those themes.",
          "claim_ids": [],
          "seat_id": "simon-sinek"
        },
        {
          "evidence_id": "ev-simon-sinek-find-your-why-c005",
          "source_id": "src-simon-sinek-find-your-why",
          "source_version": "858619f10c91dcd805d57e021c40d538a7507472bfbee7b6f97c8f0a4a2f8887",
          "locator": {
            "kind": "section",
            "value": "item 5: Non-Negotiable Principles"
          },
          "kind": "concept",
          "mark": "paraphrase",
          "original_speaker": null,
          "excerpt": null,
          "paraphrase": "A WHY is discovered, not created. It describes who a person or organization already is at their natural best; it is not an aspiration, a market position, or a statement of who they would like to become.",
          "claim_ids": [],
          "seat_id": "simon-sinek"
        },
        {
          "evidence_id": "ev-simon-sinek-find-your-why-c006",
          "source_id": "src-simon-sinek-find-your-why",
          "source_version": "858619f10c91dcd805d57e021c40d538a7507472bfbee7b6f97c8f0a4a2f8887",
          "locator": {
            "kind": "section",
            "value": "item 6: The Transformation Arc"
          },
          "kind": "concept",
          "mark": "paraphrase",
          "original_speaker": null,
          "excerpt": null,
          "paraphrase": "The transformation arc runs from operating without a clear purpose, through the split that arrives as success shifts focus from WHY to WHAT, toward the fulfillment of working for a cause larger than the task list.",
          "claim_ids": [],
          "seat_id": "simon-sinek"
        },
        {
          "evidence_id": "ev-simon-sinek-find-your-why-c007",
          "source_id": "src-simon-sinek-find-your-why",
          "source_version": "858619f10c91dcd805d57e021c40d538a7507472bfbee7b6f97c8f0a4a2f8887",
          "locator": {
            "kind": "section",
            "value": "item 7: Coaching Questions"
          },
          "kind": "concept",
          "mark": "paraphrase",
          "original_speaker": null,
          "excerpt": null,
          "paraphrase": "Partner questions are feeling-focused and story-specific: how an experience felt, what was loved about it, and what contribution the teller made to something beyond themselves.",
          "claim_ids": [],
          "seat_id": "simon-sinek"
        },
        {
          "evidence_id": "ev-simon-sinek-find-your-why-c008",
          "source_id": "src-simon-sinek-find-your-why",
          "source_version": "858619f10c91dcd805d57e021c40d538a7507472bfbee7b6f97c8f0a4a2f8887",
          "locator": {
            "kind": "section",
            "value": "item 8: Tools, Exercises, and Practices"
          },
          "kind": "concept",
          "mark": "paraphrase",
          "original_speaker": null,
          "excerpt": null,
          "paraphrase": "Exercises include Peaks and Valleys: draw a timeline, plot fulfilling memories above the line and painful ones below, then read the themes across both, because the WHY shows up in the hard stories as well as the happy ones.",
          "claim_ids": [],
          "seat_id": "simon-sinek"
        },
        {
          "evidence_id": "ev-simon-sinek-find-your-why-c009",
          "source_id": "src-simon-sinek-find-your-why",
          "source_version": "858619f10c91dcd805d57e021c40d538a7507472bfbee7b6f97c8f0a4a2f8887",
          "locator": {
            "kind": "section",
            "value": "item 9: Objection Handling and Resistance"
          },
          "kind": "concept",
          "mark": "paraphrase",
          "original_speaker": null,
          "excerpt": null,
          "paraphrase": "The objection that WHY work is fluffy is answered on the book's own terms: if the biology of decision-making is fluffy, then this is fluff, because the WHY sits at the center of how humans actually decide and trust.",
          "claim_ids": [],
          "seat_id": "simon-sinek"
        },
        {
          "evidence_id": "ev-simon-sinek-find-your-why-c010",
          "source_id": "src-simon-sinek-find-your-why",
          "source_version": "858619f10c91dcd805d57e021c40d538a7507472bfbee7b6f97c8f0a4a2f8887",
          "locator": {
            "kind": "section",
            "value": "item 10: Author Voice and Language"
          },
          "kind": "concept",
          "mark": "paraphrase",
          "original_speaker": null,
          "excerpt": null,
          "paraphrase": "The writing voice is optimistic, encouraging, and service-oriented, uses an inclusive we, stays conversational while remaining direct, and leans on metaphor and visual structure to make the method memorable.",
          "claim_ids": [],
          "seat_id": "simon-sinek"
        },
        {
          "evidence_id": "ev-simon-sinek-find-your-why-c012",
          "source_id": "src-simon-sinek-find-your-why",
          "source_version": "858619f10c91dcd805d57e021c40d538a7507472bfbee7b6f97c8f0a4a2f8887",
          "locator": {
            "kind": "section",
            "value": "item 12: The Repeatable Execution System"
          },
          "kind": "concept",
          "mark": "paraphrase",
          "original_speaker": null,
          "excerpt": null,
          "paraphrase": "The repeatable system: secure an objective partner who has not heard your stories, gather more stories than you need, tell the specific ones, identify themes together, draft the statement, then refine it against the HOWs.",
          "claim_ids": [],
          "seat_id": "simon-sinek"
        },
        {
          "evidence_id": "ev-simon-sinek-find-your-why-c013",
          "source_id": "src-simon-sinek-find-your-why",
          "source_version": "858619f10c91dcd805d57e021c40d538a7507472bfbee7b6f97c8f0a4a2f8887",
          "locator": {
            "kind": "section",
            "value": "item 13: The Quality Bar"
          },
          "kind": "concept",
          "mark": "paraphrase",
          "original_speaker": null,
          "excerpt": null,
          "paraphrase": "The quality bar for a WHY statement is one simple, clear sentence in the form: to [contribution] so that [impact]. Simple does not mean easy; one sentence is the lowest common denominator that keeps the statement usable.",
          "claim_ids": [],
          "seat_id": "simon-sinek"
        },
        {
          "evidence_id": "ev-simon-sinek-find-your-why-c014",
          "source_id": "src-simon-sinek-find-your-why",
          "source_version": "858619f10c91dcd805d57e021c40d538a7507472bfbee7b6f97c8f0a4a2f8887",
          "locator": {
            "kind": "section",
            "value": "item 14: Non-Negotiable Execution Rules"
          },
          "kind": "concept",
          "mark": "paraphrase",
          "original_speaker": null,
          "excerpt": null,
          "paraphrase": "Process rules: never discover alone, and never use aspirational language. The statement and its HOWs express who you are at your natural best, not who you want to become someday.",
          "claim_ids": [],
          "seat_id": "simon-sinek"
        },
        {
          "evidence_id": "ev-simon-sinek-find-your-why-c015",
          "source_id": "src-simon-sinek-find-your-why",
          "source_version": "858619f10c91dcd805d57e021c40d538a7507472bfbee7b6f97c8f0a4a2f8887",
          "locator": {
            "kind": "section",
            "value": "item 15: Failure Patterns"
          },
          "kind": "concept",
          "mark": "paraphrase",
          "original_speaker": null,
          "excerpt": null,
          "paraphrase": "Discovery fails in predictable ways: the storyteller tries to play both roles and identify their own themes, or the stories stay general and likable instead of specific, so no real theme can surface.",
          "claim_ids": [],
          "seat_id": "simon-sinek"
        },
        {
          "evidence_id": "ev-simon-sinek-find-your-why-c016",
          "source_id": "src-simon-sinek-find-your-why",
          "source_version": "858619f10c91dcd805d57e021c40d538a7507472bfbee7b6f97c8f0a4a2f8887",
          "locator": {
            "kind": "section",
            "value": "item 16: Decision Logic"
          },
          "kind": "concept",
          "mark": "paraphrase",
          "original_speaker": null,
          "excerpt": null,
          "paraphrase": "Decision logic is a two-step filter: first, does this decision or opportunity align with the WHY; second, does it align with the HOWs, the specific guiding principles that prove the WHY in action.",
          "claim_ids": [],
          "seat_id": "simon-sinek"
        },
        {
          "evidence_id": "ev-simon-sinek-find-your-why-c017",
          "source_id": "src-simon-sinek-find-your-why",
          "source_version": "858619f10c91dcd805d57e021c40d538a7507472bfbee7b6f97c8f0a4a2f8887",
          "locator": {
            "kind": "section",
            "value": "item 17: Self-Review Protocol"
          },
          "kind": "concept",
          "mark": "paraphrase",
          "original_speaker": null,
          "excerpt": null,
          "paraphrase": "The self-review is the Friends Exercise: ask the people closest to you what specifically about you made them choose the friendship, and check whether their answers match the themes in your draft statement.",
          "claim_ids": [],
          "seat_id": "simon-sinek"
        },
        {
          "evidence_id": "ev-simon-sinek-find-your-why-c018",
          "source_id": "src-simon-sinek-find-your-why",
          "source_version": "858619f10c91dcd805d57e021c40d538a7507472bfbee7b6f97c8f0a4a2f8887",
          "locator": {
            "kind": "section",
            "value": "item 18: Definition of Done"
          },
          "kind": "concept",
          "mark": "paraphrase",
          "original_speaker": null,
          "excerpt": null,
          "paraphrase": "Discovery is done when the statement is drafted in the to-so-that form and rests on specific origin stories, at least five or six shared in the session and more gathered, rather than on adjectives chosen in a meeting.",
          "claim_ids": [],
          "seat_id": "simon-sinek"
        },
        {
          "evidence_id": "ev-simon-sinek-find-your-why-c019",
          "source_id": "src-simon-sinek-find-your-why",
          "source_version": "858619f10c91dcd805d57e021c40d538a7507472bfbee7b6f97c8f0a4a2f8887",
          "locator": {
            "kind": "section",
            "value": "item 19: The Amateur-to-Expert Gap"
          },
          "kind": "concept",
          "mark": "paraphrase",
          "original_speaker": null,
          "excerpt": null,
          "paraphrase": "The amateur-to-expert gap is specificity: amateurs tell general stories, experts tell specific moments with sensory and emotional detail, and only the specific stories carry themes a partner can find.",
          "claim_ids": [],
          "seat_id": "simon-sinek"
        },
        {
          "evidence_id": "ev-simon-sinek-find-your-why-c020",
          "source_id": "src-simon-sinek-find-your-why",
          "source_version": "858619f10c91dcd805d57e021c40d538a7507472bfbee7b6f97c8f0a4a2f8887",
          "locator": {
            "kind": "section",
            "value": "item 20: Professional Application"
          },
          "kind": "concept",
          "mark": "paraphrase",
          "original_speaker": null,
          "excerpt": null,
          "paraphrase": "Professionally, the method applies to hiring and talent work: recruit people who believe what the organization believes, cultural fit around the WHY, rather than hiring for skills alone and hoping purpose follows.",
          "claim_ids": [],
          "seat_id": "simon-sinek"
        }
      ]
    }
  ]
}
